{
  "note": "The metropolis you reach by metro, redone after a night walk round Shenzhen Bay and rebuilt round its station (wave 4). `station` is the entrance back in the town square; `place` is the district itself, in its own local metres (x east, z south, the bay to the north, the station at the south end of the boulevard), swapped in wholesale the same way an interior is. `walk` lists the ground you can stand on as rectangles [x0, x1, z0, z1]: downtown and its pedestrian boulevard (步行街), the promenade along the bay, the hill side west of downtown (the hill itself is src/content/hill.json), 美食街 west of the station, the ground round the station with 站前广场 in front of it, 中心广场 and the business district east of downtown, the way from there to the promenade, and 城市公园 south of the station. `farClip` and `haze` [start, end] are how far the camera sees here and where the sky-coloured haze begins and closes in. `land` is the ground round the bay as [x0, x1, z0, z1, top], its edges on the water the sea walls; `paving` the streets and squares laid on it ([x0, x1, z0, z1] and a colour where it is not the city's stone: the park's lawn), and `pattern` what is laid into the paving (a band [x0, x1, z0, z1, colour, top] or a disc {disc: [x, z, r], color, top}, each a few millimetres above what it lies on). Towers, props, the promenade and its lit path, the skyline across the bay and the blocks round the edge are authored here so the layout can be checked without running the game; `leds` on a tower asks for running light bands (`bands`, heights), lit corners (`edges`), a colour-washed crown (`crown`, one of three washes), a washed screen on its front (`screen`), two light lines up its front (`stripes`) and big lit characters (`text`, each a signs.json entry). The gate at the end of the avenue carries a couplet down its posts (`couplet`, first line then second), the first line on the left as you face it from either side, so it reads left to right like the words across the top. `edges` are the low walls [x0, x1, z0, z1] where the ground ends over open land. A tower with a `form` is one of the near side's buildings (src/world/city.js `building`): a `podium` {h, style: colonnade, books, lobby, shopfront, cafe, store, marquee or stone} with its door (`door.x` along the front) and `canopy` (glass, slab, wave, marquee or awning), then `tiers` stepping in above it, each {to: the height of its top, inset from the footprint, skin: curtain, piers, ribbons, fins, louvres, balconies, diagrid, screen, bow or garden (a sky garden, which stands where the tiers below and above it overlap), windows, dx/dz to shift it}, and a `crown` (lantern, stepped, fins, helipad, sail, garden, pavilion or slope); its `leds` say which glazing its rooms glow through (`windows`, one of src/world/leds.js GLAZING), the colours of its outlines, uplights and neon sign, and its media wall (`text`); `door: false` on a form draws no way in (a building nobody enters). A tower's `id` is the `city:<id>` its rooms name as their `building`, and its `wings` [{id, x, z, w, d, h}] are the volumes, in its own frame (front on +z), holding a room behind or beside its main one (the room whose id the wing carries), in stone with, where it has a `sign`, a lit shop window and its name in neon. `doors` are the city's doors {room, x, z, label}, each on the pavement just in front of its building's entrance; the rooms return to the city with their own `returnSpawn`. Props besides the street furniture: `pool` (a long pool of still water with jets, w by d), `fountain` (a round basin, `radius`), `pond` (w by d with rounded ends, `lotus` [x, z, flowering] on it), `pavilion`, `flowerbed` (w by d), `rockery`, `shopfront` (a small shop w by d by h, its `sign` in neon, an `awning` in two colours), `arch` (a gateway `span` wide with its `text` lit on both faces), and `citytree`, which may be any of the town's `tree` kinds.",
